<沿革內容><![CDATA[1.Enacted and promulgated a total sixteen articles of the Act on March 31, 1947
2.Amended and promulgated a total sixteen articles of the Act on April 22, 1947
3.Amended and promulgated a total seveneen articles of the Act on December 25, 1947
4.Amended and promulgated Article 3, Article 5, and Article 15 of the Act on May 13, 1948
5.Amended and promulgated Article 3 and Article 15 of the Act by the Presidential Order on March 21, 1949
6.Amended and promulgated Article 5 of the Act by the Presidential Order on November 20, 1952
7.Amended and promulgated Article 3 of the Act by the Presidential Order No.3666 on November 20, 1980
8.Amended and promulgated a total fifteen articles of the Act by the Presidential Order No.09900024171 on February 3, 2010, and enacted on January 1, 2012
9.Amended and promulgated Article 3, Article 4, and Article 15 of the Act by the Presidential Order No.11100003361 on January 19, 2022
10.Amended and promulgated Article 3 of the Act by the Presidential Order No.11200033891 on April 26, 2023]]></沿革內容>
<前言><![CDATA[]]></前言>
<法規內容>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 1</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Act is enacted in accordance with Article 61 of the Constitutional Law.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 2</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan shall exercise the powers granted by the Constitutional Law.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 3</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the Ministries as follows:
１.the Ministry of the Interior;
２.the Ministry of Foreign Affairs;
３.the Ministry of National Defense;
４.the Ministry of Finance;
５.the Ministry of Education;
６.the Ministry of Justice;
７.the Ministry of Economic Affairs;
８.the Ministry of Transportation and Communications;
９.the Ministry of Labor;
10.the Ministry of Agriculture;
11.the Ministry of Health and Welfare;
12.the Ministry of Environment;
13.the Ministry of Culture; and
14.the Ministry of Digital Affairs.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 4</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the Councils or Commissions as follows:
１.the National Development Council;
２.the National Science and Technology Council.;
３.the Mainland Affairs Council;
４.the Financial Supervisory Commission;
５.the Ocean Affairs Council;
６.the Overseas Community Affairs Council;
７.the Veterans Affairs Council;
８.the Council of Indigenous Peoples; and
９.the Hakka Affairs Council.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 5</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan shall have seven to nine Ministers without Portfolio, specially appointed.
The Ministers without Portfolio may hold concurrent positions as the Ministers of the Commissions or the Councils mentioned in the preceding Article.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 6</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the Directorate-General of Budget, Accounting and Statistics and the Directorate-General of Personnel Administration.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 7</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the Central Bank of the Republic of China (Taiwan).]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 8</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the National Palace Museum.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 9</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan establishes the independent administrative institutions equivalent to the second-level agencies of the Central Government:
1.the Central Election Commission;
2.the Fair Trade Commission; and
3.the National Communications Commission.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 10</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan Premier shall generally manage and govern all the affairs, and direct and supervise the affiliate agencies and the personnel thereof.
In the event that Premier fails to perform his duties for any reason, the duties shall devolve on Vice Premier.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 11</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan Premier may invite or appoint any relevant person to attend the Executive Yuan meetings.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 12</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Executive Yuan shall have one Secretary-General, specially appointed, to manage the general staff affairs, and two Deputy Secretaries-General, one of whom shall be a political appointee of equivalent ranking to Senior fourteenth grade and shall assist Secretary-General with the staff affairs of the Executive Yuan.
The Executive Yuan shall have one spokesperson, specially appointed, who may be held concurrently by a political appointee in charge of press release and communication.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 13</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The official ranks, grades, and headcounts of personnel at the Executive Yuan shall be regulated by a separate Personnel Establishment Table.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 14</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[For the purpose of managing a specific affair, the Executive Yuan may establish an internal dedicated unit.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 15</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The Act shall take into effect on January 1, 2012.
The effective date of the amended Articles of the Law shall be set by the Executive Yuan.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
</法規內容>
</法規>
